Inside runBatch() find "let batchCost = 0;" (~line 1660) and insert "let malformedCount = 0;" directly below it. This variable is scoped to runBatch() and is initialised fresh on every run -- it is NOT accumulated across multiple batch invocations. BEFORE: "let batchCost = 0;

    const total = batchItems.length;". AFTER: "let batchCost = 0;
    let malformedCount = 0;

    const total = batchItems.length;". Reference: deltas.md Delta 1, implementation.md Step 2, tasks.md T-002, specs/malformed-ndjson-counter/spec.md REQ-MNC-01.

Locate the outer catch at the bottom of runBatch() (~lines 1789-1792). BEFORE (remove entirely): "} catch (err) { batchProgressLabel.textContent = "Error: " + (err.message || err); batchProgress.classList.remove("hidden"); }". AFTER: "} catch (err) { if (err.name === "AbortError") return; // handled by cancel flow (APP-005)
  showGlobalError("Batch failed: " + err.message);
  batchProgressBar.classList.add("progress-bar--error");
  batchProgress.classList.remove("hidden");
} finally {
  btnBatchRun.disabled = false;
}". The finally block must be the last thing before runBatch() closing brace. The early return on AbortError still triggers finally (design.md Decision 2). Reference: deltas.md Delta 4, implementation.md Step 6, tasks.md T-006, specs/batch-error-path/spec.md REQ-BEP-01 through REQ-BEP-04.

In app.js, locate "let batchResultItems = [];" at IIFE scope (~line 1636). Insert "let batchAbortController = null;" on the line immediately after. BEFORE: "let batchItems       = [];
let batchResultItems = [];". AFTER: "let batchItems       = [];
let batchResultItems = [];
let batchAbortController = null;". MUST be at IIFE scope -- NOT inside runBatch(). Initial value is null so no abort fires before the first run. Both runBatch() and the click handler closure need this reference. Reference: deltas.md Delta 1, implementation.md Step 1, tasks.md T-002, specs/batch-abort-controller/spec.md REQ-BAC-01, design.md Decision 1.

Inside runBatch(), insert "batchAbortController = new AbortController();" as the absolute first statement, BEFORE "btnBatchRun.disabled = true". BEFORE: "async function runBatch() {
  btnBatchRun.disabled = true;". AFTER: "async function runBatch() {
  batchAbortController = new AbortController();
  btnBatchRun.disabled = true;". A fresh controller is required on every invocation -- an AbortController can only be aborted once and stale signals from a previous cancelled run MUST NOT affect a new run. By placing this before the Cancel button becomes visible, the controller is always ready when the button can be clicked. Reference: deltas.md Delta 2, implementation.md Step 2, tasks.md T-003, specs/batch-abort-controller/spec.md REQ-BAC-02, design.md Decision 2.

Locate fetch(`${base}/batch`, {...}) call inside runBatch() (~line 1665). Add "signal: batchAbortController.signal," as the last property. BEFORE: "const resp = await fetch(`${base}/batch`, {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify(payload),
});". AFTER: add "signal: batchAbortController.signal," before the closing "});". Without the signal the fetch is uncancellable. The server-side /batch route in src/ai-powered/server/routes.ts already respects the AbortSignal -- this single addition terminates both the client fetch and the server-side SSE stream. No server changes are required. Reference: deltas.md Delta 3, implementation.md Step 3, tasks.md T-004, specs/batch-abort-controller/spec.md REQ-BAC-03, proposal.md What Changes.

In runBatch(), immediately after "btnBatchRun.disabled = true;", add "btnCancelBatch.style.display = "inline-flex";". BEFORE: "btnBatchRun.disabled = true;
  batchProgressBar.style.width = "0%";". AFTER: "btnBatchRun.disabled = true;
  btnCancelBatch.style.display = "inline-flex";
  batchProgressBar.style.width = "0%";". Use "inline-flex" (not "block") -- matches .btn display convention (design.md Decision 5). The button must be visible only while the batch fetch is active. Reference: deltas.md Delta 4, implementation.md Step 4, tasks.md T-005, specs/cancel-button-ux/spec.md REQ-CBU-02.

In the finally block of runBatch() (~line 1795), add "btnCancelBatch.style.display = "none";" after "btnBatchRun.disabled = false;". BEFORE: "} finally {
  btnBatchRun.disabled = false;
}". AFTER: "} finally {
  btnBatchRun.disabled = false;
  btnCancelBatch.style.display = "none";
}". The finally block guarantees the Cancel button is hidden in ALL three exit paths -- success, genuine error, and cancellation. Reference: deltas.md Delta 4, implementation.md Step 4, tasks.md T-006, specs/cancel-button-ux/spec.md REQ-CBU-02 and REQ-CBU-06, design.md Decision 4.

Locate the outer catch block of runBatch() (~line 1789). Replace the App-004 stub entirely. BEFORE (remove): "} catch (err) {
  if (err.name === "AbortError") return;
  showGlobalError("Batch failed: " + err.message);
  batchProgressBar.classList.add("progress-bar--error");
  batchProgress.classList.remove("hidden");
} finally {
  btnBatchRun.disabled = false;
}". AFTER: "} catch (err) {
  if (err.name === "AbortError") {
    batchProgressLabel.textContent = `Cancelled — ${done_count} of ${total} processed`;
  } else {
    showGlobalError("Batch failed: " + err.message);
    batchProgressBar.classList.add("progress-bar--error");
    batchProgress.classList.remove("hidden");
  }
} finally {
  btnBatchRun.disabled = false;
  btnCancelBatch.style.display = "none";
}". The user cancelled intentionally -- no red banner, no red bar. Reference: deltas.md Delta 5, implementation.md Step 5, tasks.md T-008, specs/cancel-button-ux/spec.md REQ-CBU-04 and REQ-CBU-05, design.md Decision 4.

In app.js, find the DOM-ready / init section (~line 1640) where other button listeners are registered. Add: "const btnCancelBatch = document.getElementById("btn-cancel-batch");
btnCancelBatch.addEventListener("click", () => {
  batchAbortController?.abort();
});". PLACEMENT: must be outside and after runBatch is defined, but inside the IIFE so batchAbortController is in scope. Do NOT place inside runBatch() -- that would stack duplicate listeners on every run invocation (design.md Decision 3). The optional-chaining ?.abort() guards against errors when batchAbortController is still null on first page load. Reference: deltas.md Delta 7, implementation.md Step 7, tasks.md T-007, specs/batch-abort-controller/spec.md REQ-BAC-04.

In app.js, immediately before the parseMdFile JSDoc comment ("/** * Parse a Markdown shot-list file."), insert: "/** Matches an optional modality tag at the end of a Markdown heading line. */
const MODALITY_TAG_RE = /[\[(](video|image|text|audio)[\])]\s*$/i;". BEFORE: "  /**
   * Parse a Markdown shot-list file.". AFTER: "  /** Matches an optional modality tag at the end of a Markdown heading line. */
  const MODALITY_TAG_RE = /[\[(](video|image|text|audio)[\])]\s*$/i;

  /**
   * Parse a Markdown shot-list file.". The regex matches bracket [..] or paren (..) forms, is case-insensitive, and is anchored to end-of-string. Declaring it as a named constant outside the function avoids recompilation on every call and makes it reusable for tag stripping in the heading branch. Reference: deltas.md Delta 1, implementation.md Step 1, tasks.md T-001, specs/parse-md-modality R-001.

Immediately after the MODALITY_TAG_RE constant (and still before parseMdFile), insert: "  function parseHeadingModality(heading) {
    const m = MODALITY_TAG_RE.exec(heading);
    return m ? m[1].toLowerCase() : "video";
  }". This function: (1) executes MODALITY_TAG_RE against the raw heading text; (2) returns the lower-cased capture group when a tag is found (e.g., "[IMAGE]" yields "image"); (3) returns "video" when no recognised tag is present -- backward compat default. MUST NOT mutate the heading argument. Used in the heading branch (T-005) to set currentModality. See examples/parse-md-modality.js lines 48-51 for the reference implementation. Reference: deltas.md Delta 2, implementation.md Step 2, tasks.md T-002, specs/parse-md-modality R-002.

Inside parseMdFile, find the variable declarations block: "let currentName = null;
let promptLines = [];". Change to: "let currentName     = null;
let currentModality = "video";
let promptLines     = [];". currentModality follows the same section-scoped lifecycle as currentName: it is set when a heading is encountered and reset to "video" inside flush() after each item is pushed. Initialising to "video" ensures the fallback path (files with no headings at all) also produces modality: "video". Reference: deltas.md Delta 3, implementation.md Step 3, tasks.md T-003, specs/parse-md-modality R-003 and R-010.

Inside flush() in parseMdFile, find: "if (prompt) items.push({ name: currentName, prompt, modality: "video" });
prompLines = [];". Replace with: "if (prompt) items.push({ name: currentName, prompt, modality: currentModality });
currentModality = "video";
prompLines = [];". Two changes: (1) modality: "video" hardcode becomes modality: currentModality; (2) "currentModality = "video"" reset added after the push. Resetting inside flush() rather than at the heading branch ensures an empty section (heading with no prompt lines) does NOT corrupt the modality of the next section (design.md Decision 3). Reference: deltas.md Delta 3, implementation.md Step 4, tasks.md T-004, specs/parse-md-modality R-004.

Inside the for loop in parseMdFile, find: "if (headingMatch) {
  flush();
  currentName = headingMatch[1].trim();". Replace the currentName assignment with three lines: "  flush();
  const rawHeading = headingMatch[1].trim();
  currentModality  = parseHeadingModality(rawHeading);
  currentName      = rawHeading.replace(MODALITY_TAG_RE, "").trim();". (1) rawHeading preserves original text for both operations; (2) parseHeadingModality sets currentModality from the tag or "video" if absent; (3) MODALITY_TAG_RE strips the tag so the stored name is clean. Given heading "## Intro Scene [image]", result is name="Intro Scene", modality="image". Unknown tags like [3d] are NOT stripped -- MODALITY_TAG_RE only matches the 4 recognised values (specs/parse-md-modality AC-8). Reference: deltas.md Delta 3, implementation.md Step 5, tasks.md T-005, specs/parse-md-modality R-005 and R-009.

In showBatchPreflight, immediately after the labelSpan.textContent assignment (after T-052 edit), add: "const badge = document.createElement("span");
badge.className = \`modality-badge modality-badge--\${modality}\`;
badge.textContent = modality;
labelSpan.appendChild(badge);". This block MUST appear before "const em = document.createElement("em")" so child order in labelSpan is: text node → badge → em (specs/modality-badge-ux AC-25). BEFORE: "labelSpan.textContent = ...
const em = document.createElement("em");". AFTER: "labelSpan.textContent = ...
const badge = ...
badge.className = ...
badge.textContent = ...
labelSpan.appendChild(badge);
const em = document.createElement("em");". Badge is rendered for ALL modalities including the "video" default -- never omitted (R-025). Reference: deltas.md Delta 4, implementation.md Step 7, tasks.md T-007, specs/modality-badge-ux R-020.

Open integrations/web-example/index.html. Inside the <style> block (before the closing </style> tag), append the base modality badge rule: "/* Modality badges — preflight shot list */
.modality-badge {
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 0.65rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  padding: 1px 5px;
  border-radius: 3px;
  margin-left: 5px;
  vertical-align: middle;
  color: #fff;
}". All 10 properties are required by specs/modality-badge-ux R-022. Ensure the comment and rule are placed BEFORE the four colour variants (T-062). Reference: deltas.md Delta 5, implementation.md Step 8, tasks.md T-009, specs/modality-badge-ux R-022.

Immediately after the .modality-badge base rule (T-061), add: ".modality-badge--video  { background: #2563eb; }
.modality-badge--image  { background: #7c3aed; }
.modality-badge--text   { background: #16a34a; }
.modality-badge--audio  { background: #ea580c; }". Colours: video=blue (#2563eb), image=violet (#7c3aed), text=green (#16a34a), audio=orange (#ea580c). All four pass WCAG AA contrast ratio (>=4.5:1) against #fff white text (design.md Decision 6). These match the proxy endpoint convention: /video, /image, /text, /audio. Reference: deltas.md Delta 5, implementation.md Step 8, tasks.md T-010, specs/modality-badge-ux R-023.
